WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
Thank you. Good afternoon, everyone.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.270
My name is Kalin Kostadinov and I'm the manager of the City Living Lab

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.430
part of the GATE Institute in Sofia.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.190
So, first of all, before I start, I have a question.

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.760
Can you give me a show of hands of how many of you know what the

6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.030
Living Lab actually is?

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.280
Okay. I expected that.

8
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.960
So, Dubai is a great example and I think that all

9
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.680
of us should strive to get there at some point,

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.350
but how do we actually do this?

11
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.710
A Living Lab is where four very important groups come together

12
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.750
to discover problems,

13
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.670
look for solutions, and try to implement them.

14
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.720
So, first of all, in a Living Lab, the important part is to have a

15
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.390
seed. That's where all the problems stem from.

16
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.150
That's how we do discoverability

17
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.190
and then we go through research

18
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.630
so that we can actually find solutions to those problems.

19
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.670
A Living Lab should always involve companies.

20
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.640
They are an important, integral part because they are the ones that are

21
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.430
most of the time deploying the actual solutions.

22
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.080
And the most important group are the residents because they are the

23
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.430
ones consuming those new products.

24
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.910
So, the purpose of a Living Lab is to provide an infrastructure

25
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.190
where new solutions can be tested in real life,

26
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.560
not on paper. It happens very fast because it's already in

27
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.070
existing infrastructure

28
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.852
and it supports different types of companies or startups to

29
00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:03.162
scale up quickly and deploy in a city.

30
00:02:04.652 --> 00:02:09.002
So, at GATE, we started back in 2019,

31
00:02:10.292 --> 00:02:13.522
and after conversation with the municipality,

32
00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:17.562
we came to an agreement that we should cooperate

33
00:02:18.612 --> 00:02:22.972
on the digitalization priorities for the next 10 years.

34
00:02:22.972 --> 00:02:29.612
And one of the most important parts was the lab and also the

35
00:02:29.612 --> 00:02:34.082
city digital twin. So, over the years after 2020,

36
00:02:34.892 --> 00:02:39.012
we spent a lot of time on research, collecting all the data that

37
00:02:39.012 --> 00:02:44.882
the city has, and trying to figure out what is actually missing

38
00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:50.932
to do the next step so that we can actually work and find solutions

39
00:02:50.932 --> 00:02:51.882
towards the problem.

40
00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:56.812
So, at the end of the day, we decided to build an infrastructure of

41
00:02:56.812 --> 00:03:02.572
sensors, lidar, we have a drone that we're going to use to

42
00:03:02.572 --> 00:03:09.172
collect data in real time and try to use that data

43
00:03:09.172 --> 00:03:11.162
for the solutions that we're preparing.

44
00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:15.532
Now, because everybody's asking, "Oh, what happens?

45
00:03:15.532 --> 00:03:20.012
Why don't we see all this research integrated into the

46
00:03:20.012 --> 00:03:24.092
city?" Well, there are steps to it.

47
00:03:24.092 --> 00:03:29.972
We cannot get to actual production-grade solutions before we

48
00:03:29.972 --> 00:03:32.082
cooperate with companies.

49
00:03:32.492 --> 00:03:36.292
So, for instance, part of our solutions, the idea is to become

50
00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:39.002
spin-offs and then

51
00:03:41.052 --> 00:03:43.562
be implemented in the city.

52
00:03:45.532 --> 00:03:51.842
So, our living lab actually consists of over 100 sensors.

53
00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.602
We have 12 air quality

54
00:03:55.772 --> 00:04:00.092
stations that we actually recently used because the radio called us

55
00:04:00.092 --> 00:04:02.442
and said, "Look,

56
00:04:04.174 --> 00:04:06.134
there was a huge fire in Sofia.

57
00:04:06.134 --> 00:04:08.334
We want to know what the pollution was."

58
00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:12.574
So, we took the weather forecast and also data from

59
00:04:12.574 --> 00:04:16.044
the sensors, and we were able to answer

60
00:04:17.054 --> 00:04:21.734
the public, the residents of Sofia, what the pollution was.

61
00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:24.284
Was there even pollution after this fire?

62
00:04:25.174 --> 00:04:29.574
And so on. Then, we also have 60 noise sensors.

63
00:04:29.574 --> 00:04:33.574
Those are really important because we can measure how much noise the

64
00:04:33.574 --> 00:04:35.484
traffic produces in Sofia.

65
00:04:36.454 --> 00:04:40.044
And we can use that information

66
00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.644
to plan better cities.

67
00:04:44.494 --> 00:04:48.654
We also have 50 pedestrian counters that we're using in different

68
00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:52.574
walkability analyses. Whenever there is an event,

69
00:04:52.574 --> 00:04:55.974
we see where people are gathering, which routes they're taking,

70
00:04:55.974 --> 00:04:58.644
and this also helps for better planning.

71
00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:03.654
We also have one intersection in Sofia at which we have six

72
00:05:03.654 --> 00:05:07.964
lidar sensors. And they collect data about traffic,

73
00:05:08.454 --> 00:05:13.644
and we do analysis, and we simulate different scenarios of how to

74
00:05:14.214 --> 00:05:15.844
improve the traffic flow.

75
00:05:17.054 --> 00:05:20.974
And all of this is being done, and we're trying to cooperate as much

76
00:05:20.974 --> 00:05:22.764
as possible with the municipality.

77
00:05:24.454 --> 00:05:29.734
So, bringing everything together, we take the data that's already

78
00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.564
existing in Sofia.

79
00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.964
We're taking all the live data from the sensors,

80
00:05:36.614 --> 00:05:39.734
and also street network, bars, trees, everything,

81
00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:43.294
and we bring it together into one space.

82
00:05:43.294 --> 00:05:44.804
This is the digital twin.

83
00:05:45.214 --> 00:05:50.294
So, we create different layers of data, where those layers usually

84
00:05:50.294 --> 00:05:54.694
are coming from different places, and when we combine them,

85
00:05:54.694 --> 00:05:58.204
we manage to do many new types of analysis.

86
00:05:59.054 --> 00:06:03.014
So, we can know what is the cause for

87
00:06:03.014 --> 00:06:07.215
traffic delays. When people travel to work, why don't they use more

88
00:06:07.215 --> 00:06:10.885
public transport? Do they miss some bus stops somewhere?

89
00:06:12.415 --> 00:06:16.935
And so on. So, now at this stage, we're trying mostly to work with

90
00:06:16.935 --> 00:06:21.325
companies. Last week I was attending an event

91
00:06:22.295 --> 00:06:25.725
that's part of the European Network of Living Labs.

92
00:06:26.495 --> 00:06:31.015
And there they told us that the future, because nowadays European

93
00:06:31.015 --> 00:06:34.135
projects already know a lot about the living labs,

94
00:06:34.135 --> 00:06:36.085
there are a lot of living labs already existing.

95
00:06:37.335 --> 00:06:43.175
And now the goal is to use those labs as a test bed for new

96
00:06:43.175 --> 00:06:47.415
companies or existing ones when they want to experiment and create

97
00:06:47.415 --> 00:06:51.605
new solutions. So,

98
00:06:53.055 --> 00:06:58.095
what's the idea? Because we've spent working on the living lab maybe 4,

99
00:06:58.095 --> 00:07:01.365
5 years now, and we learned a lot of lessons.

100
00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:08.695
First of all, we think that a living lab should also be co-owned by

101
00:07:08.695 --> 00:07:11.485
the city because the living lab allows

102
00:07:13.495 --> 00:07:15.965
for the creation of hyper-local solutions.

103
00:07:18.295 --> 00:07:23.885
And also there should always be research institutions,

104
00:07:24.455 --> 00:07:28.735
universities need to have access to the lab so that they

105
00:07:28.735 --> 00:07:31.045
can create innovations.

106
00:07:31.895 --> 00:07:36.415
And also the last point are businesses so that they can bring use

107
00:07:36.415 --> 00:07:40.655
cases, they can test them, and they can deploy them afterwards and

108
00:07:40.655 --> 00:07:43.525
scale them up. So, thank you very much.

109
00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:45.275
And
